  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Gravitational force of attraction exists in all the places in the universe. This is the force of attraction between any two substances that are having a mass of their own.&nbsp;</p><p>Every object in the universe attracts every other object with a force which is proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them.</p><p>The weight of a body placed at the centre of the earth is zero. This is because acceleration due to gravity is zero at the centre and hence weight&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is zero at the centre. Thus, both statements are true.</p>",
